dron ander sepazate controlff\nthe planes and personnel to be turned over to the military.\nwe decided that the\n\"charter\" trip was conneroial we would\ntako it but it we decided it was military we would ask that\nthe trip be made by one of the military squadron pilote.\nThe Managing Director felt that our plan would cost. him\ntoo much loss of face and tried to get ue to compromiee.\nstalled long enough to arrange for ONAG to finance the evacu-\nation of all american women and children of CHAO pereonnel,\nsecured payment of base salaries of all Amerioan pilots and\nground personnel tor the whole month of August and also the\nbonue to all Do-8 pilots which was due in July but had not\nbeen paid.\nI also tried to collect money owing PAA but was\nunsucceseful in getting anything but promises.\non saturday ang. 21st I had a talk with Mr. 0. E. Gauss,\nConsul General, and after a full discussion of the whole situ-\nation we decided that further participation in the affaire of\nONAC could lead only to trouble.\nI assured ur. Gause that\nroulă withdraw from the \"directing, supervising or instruoting\nfrom the ground\" to quote lie own\nLetter to me copy of whiel\nis attached hereto.\nI aleo had a talk with Judge Helmiok of\nthe Amerioan Court\nfor China, who heartily approved of our\ndecision and stated moat emphatically that the law would be\nstrictly enforced, violators woold be prosecuted to the",
